{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791794427,"nonce":"YMTAtVayog1+DDODgqd7e0IuODU=","title":"Enum constructors erase their own type parameters and infer only from the first argument","message":"TestGADT declares EBinop\u003cC\u003e(op:Binop\u003cC,T\u003e,e1:Expr\u003cC\u003e,e2:Expr\u003cC\u003e):Expr\u003cT\u003e. The recursive-descent parser reads C then replaces its occurrences in payload annotations with Dynamic and discards the constructor type-parameter list. The explicit result annotation still names C in smaller cases, where lowering treats it as a class name. The AST has no constructor type-parameter field. The nom parser does not consume the list at all.\n\nReduced native-valid case: enum Kind\u003cT\u003e { FloatKind(value:Float):Kind\u003cFloat\u003e; } enum Wrapped\u003cT\u003e { Wrap\u003cC\u003e(kind:Kind\u003cC\u003e,value:C):Wrapped\u003cC\u003e; }. Wrap(FloatKind(2.5),2.5) should have type Wrapped\u003cFloat\u003e. Native Haxe 4.3.6 --interp passes the compile-time type assertion and generic payload read. Frozen Rayzor v53 fails the constructor type assertion. Reproducer target/conformance-checkpoint/gadt-probe/GadtProbe.hx; log gadt-probe-v53.log.\n\nLowering also infers a generic enum constructor result from only its first argument, even if that argument is another enum or if a constructor reorders multiple result parameters. Preserve and scope the declared parameters, infer bindings structurally from all payload arguments, and substitute into the constructor's declared result. Branch-level GADT refinement is separate work.","files":null}]}